<code>assert element != null => element.equals(this.peek());</code>

This assert statement checks that if the element added to the queue is not null, it will be equal to the last element in the queue after the operation. Note that `peek()` returns the head of the queue, but since the queue is circular and the last added element becomes the head when the queue is full, this condition effectively checks that the last added element is now the head of the queue.
